			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — Cocoon SCM args, Mountain URI fixes, Output typed window, Sky bridge routing\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 034b8ea8, integrating fixes across five Element components.\n\nCocoon replaces the blanket `arguments` strip in `SanitizeResourceState` with `ProjectArg` — a shallow copy preserving only the safe primitive fields SCM resource commands consult. Cycles from the Repository back-reference are naturally excluded. SCM resource commands now navigate to the intended file across all git integration features.\n\nMountain reconstructs full URIs from vscode.Uri POJOs with a fallback priority chain — `external` → `scheme+authority+path+query+fragment` → `fsPath` → bare `path` — so non-file URIs like `rust-analyzer-diagnostics-view:` resolve correctly. The `$provideTreeChildren` timeout is bumped from 5s to 15s for cold multi-repo scans. `localPty:processBinary` is routed through `TerminalSendText` so clipboard paste and escape sequences reach the PTY. `outputChannel.hide` is forwarded to Sky as `sky://output/show { visible: false }`.\n\nOutput splits `InvokeWindowCommand` into `StartDragging` and `ToggleMaximize`, each preferring the typed `@tauri-apps/api/window` JS API before falling back to raw `core.invoke` with an explicit label payload. Drag and maximize now work reliably under Tauri 2.x.\n\nSky normalises output channel payload field names across Mountain's coalescer, legacy append, and Cocoon forwarding paths. Routes `sky://notification/show` through `INotificationService.notify()` for live toast rendering, calls `monaco.editor.setModelLanguage()` for `sky://languages/setDocumentLanguage`, derives per-repo SCM display labels from `rootUri` basename in multi-repo workspaces, and routes progress through `IProgressService.withProgress()` with DOM fallback during early boot.\n\nMaintain advances the Rust API documentation submodule pin — 362 files, +4951/−1426 lines of regenerated rustdoc.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application root — pure submodule pointer update.",
