			"Message": "refactor(Land): Align telemetry env vars with Pipe/Emit naming\n\nRename the telemetry configuration environment variables from `OTLPEndpoint`/`OTLPEnabled` to `Pipe`/`Emit` across all Land shell scripts and build configuration, completing the coordinated field rename that began in the Element submodule.\n\nPostHogCapture.sh updates its internal variable references, fallback defaults, and documentation header to use `Pipe` for the OTLP HTTP collector address and `Emit` for the Jaeger enable/disable toggle. TierEnvironment.sh renames the entries in `_LandSnapshotKeys`, runtime key allow-lists, and tier-file snapshot keys so the renamed variables are correctly captured and persisted across environment tiers. turbo.json updates the global `env` passthrough list so both `Pipe` and `Emit` are forwarded to Turborepo task runtimes.\n\nThis eliminates the discrepancy between the Element submodule's convention (Cocoon, Wind, Common, Worker) and the Land root's shell scripts and build cache configuration.",
